        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add bridge rich links",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add canonical URL-only Apple preview sends with `imsg send-rich --url <url>` and RPC `send.rich` using one chat target plus `url`\n- fetch LinkPresentation metadata in the CLI process; the injected Messages helper performs no network access\n- use a dedicated `send-rich-link` bridge action and action-specific capability so stale helpers fail before fetching or sending\n- keep non-URL `send-rich` behavior unchanged for text, effects, replies, subjects, formatting, and attachments\n\n## Maintainer rewrite\n\nThis branch was rewritten on current `main`, preserving Omar's feature direction while tightening the public and private-runtime contracts:\n\n- strict HTTP(S), host, credential, title, target, service, and modifier validation\n- one eight-second preparation deadline with cancellation propagation and staged-image cleanup\n- metadata-only fallback when metadata/image preparation fails; no plain-message downgrade\n- accepted images limited to JPEG/PNG/WebP, one frame, 2 MiB, 4096x4096, and 16 megapixels before decode/staging\n- SHA-256-bound image descriptors and component-wise `openat`/`O_NOFOLLOW` reads from the real user's Messages attachment tree\n- fd identity checks, MIME/dimension verification, and a private 0700/0600 `O_EXCL` snapshot before IMCore sees the file\n- balloon construction before daemon transfer registration, avoiding orphaned transfers on archive/KVC failure\n- exact `chat_identifier`/`chat_guid` lookup with iMessage preference when SMS and iMessage rows share an identifier\n- helper input type validation so malformed bridge JSON cannot crash Messages\n- per-architecture Swift scratch paths and `--show-bin-path` packaging to prevent stale universal slices\n- docs, skill example, release changelog, and contributor credit\n\n## Verification on `79a1a26`\n\n- `DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer make test` — pass\n- `DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer make lint` — pass; 8 existing warnings, 0 serious\n- `make build-dylib` — pass; one existing Foundation deprecation warning\n- Clang static analyzer — pass with 0 findings\n- universal release build — CLI `x86_64 arm64`; helper `x86_64 arm64 arm64e`; strict codesign verification passed\n- focused rich-link preparation/CLI/RPC/helper regressions — pass, including animation rejection, stale-helper version skew, cancellation, aliases/modifiers, SMS/iMessage ambiguity, and poll construction\n- structured Codex AutoReview — clean; no accepted/actionable findings\n- source-blind behavior validation — canonical help, CLI fail-closed, and RPC fail-closed clauses pass; live rendering blocked without a SIP-disabled bridge host\n- source-blind validation also reproduced the existing global CLI behavior where parse/command errors stay plain text under `--json`; that router-wide issue is outside this PR\n\n## Merge gate\n\nDo not merge until the rewritten exact head has receiver-visible proof on a SIP-disabled bridge host for:\n\n1. title/domain/image rich card rendering\n2. metadata-only card rendering\n3. persisted URL balloon and hidden-transfer shape\n4. an adjacent native poll send to rule out shared balloon-builder regression\n\nGitHub macOS and Linux CI must also pass on the rewritten head.\n\nThanks @omarshahine for the feature and the original runtime investigation.\n",
